<title>ARGENTINA: IADB to loan Argentina $104 million,launch program.</title>
<headline>IADB to loan Argentina $104 million,launch program.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-08-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Inter American Development Bank (IADB) will grant Monday a $104 million loan to improve Argentine ports efficiency, state-run agency Telam said Sunday.</p>
<p>At the same time the bank will launch a $370 million program to help poor young people to get a job, Telam added quoting government sources.</p>
<p>The loan to improve ports efficiency through better transport systems and logistic will be signed by IADB President Enrique Iglesias and Argentine Economy Minister Roque Fernandez.</p>
<p>((--Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
